>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_safe_solver`

``` hol4
simpLib.add_safe_solver : Traverse.ssolver -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a named safe solver to a simpset.

Safe solvers are the final solvers of `GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = true}`; they
are never used for side conditions.
`add_safe_solver solver ss` appends `solver` unless `ss` already has a
safe solver of the same name. Solvers are described under
[`simpLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpLib.add_unsafe_solver).

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>> val decide = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE} : Traverse.ssolver;
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_safe_solver decide bool_ss;
>> simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = true} ss [] ([], “x < x + 1”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC`](#simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC),
[`simpLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpLib.add_unsafe_solver),
[`simpLib.set_safe_solvers`](#simpLib.set_safe_solvers),
[`simpLib.safe_solver_ss`](#simpLib.safe_solver_ss).
